(There are spoilers in what follows.)

I started up a character of the priestly vocation yesterday.  On Dlvl 1,
I found a blessed potion of invisibility, so I gained that intrinsic.  On
Dlvl 2, I found a cursed lamp.  I thought, "Why would anyone curse an
ordinary lamp?"  So I #dipped it (in holy water) once, #rubbed it, and
sure enough, I saw a puff of smoke.  I #dipped it again, #rubbed it some
more, and eventually released a djinni, who gratefully granted me one wish.
I decided on a blessed +3 war hammer named Mjollnir, which I got (well, I
don't know about the plusses.)

So far, so good.  On Dlvl 4 I found the ghost of a previous incarnation of
myself, who had, among other things, a cursed long sword and a cursed
two-handed sword named Orcrist.  I repeatedly #dipped the long sword in a 
fountain which was conveniently located nearby; unfortunately, it rusted (to 
-1, I think), but eventually became a blessed long sword named Excalibur.
Better and better.

On Dlvl 5, I found an altar to Mitra (lawful) and the ghost of another
previous incarnation of myself, who had, among other things, a cursed wide
sword named Dragonbane (which I uncursed), some potions of unholy water, and 
a lot of tools (which, as I recall, came from a hardware store).  The latter 
included a cursed bag of holding.  "Aha!" I thought.  "Time for the cursed bag 
of holding trick!"

As it turned out, the first time around I got it backwards, resulting in
my posting yesterday.  I put a lot of useless stuff in the bag, blessed
it, and tried to take the stuff out, but couldn't - I couldn't carry any
more.  After a little thought I realized that the bag should be cursed
*after* all the useless stuff is placed in it, so that taking the stuff out
leads to a negative weight.  (Thanks, by the way, to all who replied to my
post.)  I figured that I should put as much stuff as I could possibly carry
in the blessed bag (a not inconsiderable amount, since I had strength 18),
to get a negative weight of greatest magnitude.  To this end, I dropped
all of my useful stuff, except for Mjollnir and the armor I was wearing.
Then I started killing various monsters and putting their stuff in my bag.
Along the way, I killed a brown pudding and ate its corpse: "You feel full
of hot air."

I had killed all the monsters on Dlvl 5 and still hadn't reached the limit
of my carrying capacity, so I transferred all my useful stuff to Dlvl 6
and started killing monsters there.  I had almost reached my goal ("You
have a little trouble lifting...") when - I stepped on a level teleport
trap and was transported to Dlvl 24!  And it was going so well!

Well, I figured I was in pretty hot water then.  I had a measly 45 hit
points (maximum) and AC 2.  On Dlvl 24, all other things being equal,
I had the life expectancy of a newt.  What's more, I had dropped all
of my food on Dlvl 6; pretty soon I was going to get hungry and faint.
(By the way, I am under the impression that praying to one's god only
leads to gastric contentment if one is already fainting.  Is this true?)
Trying to kill monsters for food was pretty much out of the question.
Time for some very careful playing...

Being invisible came in *very* handy, and having cold resistance saved my
skin, since the first monster I encountered was a white dragon ("The blast
of frost hits you!  You don't feel cold!")  I figured my best strategy was
to avoid monsters as far as possible and try to find the up stairs very
quickly.  Before that, however, I cursed my bag of holding and took
everything out (well, everything that didn't disappear).

I got to Dlvl 23 without major mishap, and found there a blessed potion of
see invisible, so I got that intrinsic (I think?).  Oh no!  A trapdoor!  Back 
to Dlvl 24.

I managed to reach the up stairs again, although at one point the white
dragon cornered me and got me down to 14 hit points.  (*Why* did I have
to leave Dragonbane upstairs?)  On Dlvl 23 I found a pair of speed boots.  
I reached the up stairs without further incident, and on Dlvl 22 I found 
a cursed scroll.

"All right," I thought.  "This could be a scroll of create monster, in which
case, if I read it I'm as good as dead.  On the other hand, it could be a
scroll of teleportation, which could save my life (or could send me to hell,
where I would burn to a crisp).  Should I read it?"

I decided to take the risk.  It was a cursed scroll of teleportation, which
sent me to Dlvl 9!  What a relief!

In the same room I was teleported into, I found a cursed potion, which I
quaffed.  "You levitate through the ceiling -more-" and there I was on
Dlvl 8.  Obviously, a potion of gain level (get it?).

I got up to Dlvl 7 without too much fuss.  There I bought a cloak
of protection, gauntlets of power, a blessed +2 splint mail, blessed +2 hard
shoes, and a helmet (I think it's an ordinary helmet, since it cost only
66 zorkmids).

Finally I got back to Dlvl 6, picked up all my stuff (how nice to be able
to carry everything) and retamed my kitten Fragonard.  My questions are:

(1) Can a magic lamp be recharged once it has been used?

(2) I currently have 2 potions of holy water and 2 potions of unholy water.
Do I need the unholy water for anything else, or should I convert it to holy
water (using the altar on Dlvl 5)?  I have a scroll of teleportation, which
I may need to curse eventually.  On the other hand, I have a cursed magic
marker, which I might use to write a cursed scroll of teleportation.

(3) The only limitation on my carrying capacity is the number of inventory
letters (a-zA-Z).  If I uncurse the bag of holding, will it eliminate this
problem?  In other words, do items in a bag of holding still take up
inventory letters?  I hope they don't; this is the only possible
justification for the tedious sequential access to items in a bag.

Thanks in advance for your help.

-- Ruchira


